`@web/canvas` provides 2D canvas drawing as a builder binding-backed runtime package. It belongs to the Builder origin family with ExternalBinding backing, so the compiler registers typed external functions and opaque types from annotated JavaScript. See @../../#package-origins-and-backing (Package origins and backing) for origin and backing rules.

`@web/canvas` ships as a skeleton. The current surface covers element management, context state, rectangles, paths, text, gradients, patterns, image drawing, image data and pixel access. It will grow as the language stabilises and the first-party packages expand.

The accepted numeric API uses I32 dimensions/indices and F64 coordinates and
measurements. That exact cutover remains pending in the profile-based Alpha
implementation. It preserves existing ranges, units, foreign contracts and
the Wasm gap rather than expanding binding support.

### Dependency roots

Bind individual symbols or the whole namespace:

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    @web/canvas get_canvas, context_2d, fill_rect

    @web/canvas
]

### Opaque types

`@web/canvas` exposes seven opaque handle types. They have no public fields, cannot be constructed with struct syntax and must not be inspected directly. You obtain them only through `@web/canvas` functions.

[table:
    [th:
        [: Type]
        [: Description]
    ]

    [td:
        [: `CanvasElement`]
        [: A `<canvas>` DOM element handle]
    ]

    [td:
        [: `Canvas2d`]
        [: A 2D rendering context handle]
    ]

    [td:
        [: `CanvasGradient`]
        [: A gradient object handle]
    ]

    [td:
        [: `CanvasPattern`]
        [: A pattern object handle]
    ]

    [td:
        [: `CanvasImage`]
        [: An image element handle]
    ]

    [td:
        [: `CanvasImageData`]
        [: An `ImageData` pixel buffer handle]
    ]

    [td:
        [: `CanvasTextMetrics`]
        [: A text measurement result handle]
    ]
]

All opaque types lower to object references in the JS backend. The Wasm backend does not support `@web/canvas` and rejects reachable calls before lowering.

